### LeetCode Username

DevangSharma

### Problem Number, Title, and Link

228. Summary Ranges https://leetcode.com/problems/summary-ranges/description

### Bug Category

Missing test case *(Incorrect/Inefficient Code getting accepted because of missing test cases)*

### Bug Description

A case where 1st element of the array is equal to -2147483648 is missing. 

here if we have 1st element equal to -2^31 which is min of integer in c++ and the next element is not consecutive, it can be any number. then the range should both start and end at first element only with -2^31 in it. 

but a code missing this is giving accpeted

### Language Used for Code

C++

### Code used for Submit/Run operation

```bash
class Solution {
public:
    vector<string> summaryRanges(vector<int>& nums) {

        vector<string> result;

        int start = INT_MIN, end = INT_MIN;

        for(int i = 0; i < nums.size(); i++) {

            if(end + 1 != nums[i]) {

                if(end != INT_MIN) {
                    string range = to_string(start);

                    if(start != end) {
                        range += "->";
                        range += to_string(end);
                    }

                    result.push_back(range);
                }

                start = nums[i];
                end = nums[i];

            } else {
                end = nums[i];
            }

            if(i == nums.size() - 1) {
                    string range = to_string(start);

                    if(start != end) {
                        range += "->";
                        range += to_string(end);
                    }

                    result.push_back(range);

            }

        }

        return result;
        
    }
};
```


### Expected behavior

for the sample test case ->  `[-2147483648,0,2,3,4,6,8,9] ` , the answer should be `["-2147483648","0","2->4","6","8->9"]` but my code gives `["0","2->4","6","8->9"]` , and still its being accepted.

the reason for this expectation is explained in bug

